  "point_definition": "Whole outer-shore area centroid, with southern stream excluded at its shore connection.",
  "identity_evidence": "The unlabelled lake north of Queensville and west of the north-south road has a small northeastern lobe above a larger western basin, a southwestern shore indentation, and a southern stream that first bends west before turning southeast toward Queensville. The original modern Brileys Lake exterior and stream212551 show the same topology. Gazetteer CAFCO lies in that closed lake; the stream is unnamed in the extract. Native enlargement resolves the small shoreline after the broad overview was insufficient. Short ink gaps and southern lettering reduce trace precision; no agreement of the entire detailed outline is claimed.",
